{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-58290","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-68615","text":"SpecPrompt Documentation"}]},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58292","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68616","marks":["bold"],"text":"Prompts are transient. Specs persist."}]}],"id":"blk-58291","kind":"quote"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58294","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68617","marks":["bold"],"text":"Part of the [&] Protocol stack"},{"id":"spn-68618","text":" · "},{"id":"spn-68619","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/ECOSYSTEM.md"}],"text":"Ecosystem overview"},{"id":"spn-68620","text":" · "},{"id":"spn-68621","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/PULSE/docs/THREE_PROTOCOL_STACK.md"}],"text":"Three-protocol stack"},{"id":"spn-68622","text":" · "},{"id":"spn-68623","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/STACK_COMPLETION.md"}],"text":"Stack status"}]}],"id":"blk-58293","kind":"quote"},{"id":"blk-58295","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68624","text":"Welcome to the documentation hub for "},{"id":"spn-68625","marks":["bold"],"text":"SpecPrompt"},{"id":"spn-68626","text":" — an open standard and toolchain for spec-driven AI development. SpecPrompt defines a Markdown-based specification format (SPEC.md) that is both human-readable and machine-parseable, serving as the source of truth for agent behavior."}]},{"id":"blk-58296","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68627","text":"SpecPrompt is the "},{"id":"spn-68628","marks":["bold"],"text":"standards layer"},{"id":"spn-68629","text":" of the [&] Protocol ecosystem — the format that bridges agent definition with execution, testing, and deployment."}]},{"id":"blk-58297","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68630","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-58298","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-68631","text":"Why SpecPrompt?"}]},{"id":"blk-58299","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68632","text":"Spec-Driven Development (SDD) has emerged as the industry consensus for AI-assisted development in 2026. GitHub Spec Kit, AWS Kiro, Cursor rules, and Next Moca ADL all use different specification formats. Teams switching tools lose context."}]},{"id":"blk-58300","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68633","text":"SpecPrompt defines the interoperable standard — a Markdown-native format that is:"}]},{"id":"blk-58301","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68634","text":"1. "},{"id":"spn-68635","marks":["bold"],"text":"Markdown-native"},{"id":"spn-68636","text":" — "},{"id":"spn-68637","marks":["code"],"text":".md"},{"id":"spn-68638","text":" files, no proprietary format 2. "},{"id":"spn-68639","marks":["bold"],"text":"Human-first"},{"id":"spn-68640","text":" — readable by any team member, parseable by any agent 3. "},{"id":"spn-68641","marks":["bold"],"text":"Versioned"},{"id":"spn-68642","text":" — lives in git. Branching, diffing, merging. 4. "},{"id":"spn-68643","marks":["bold"],"text":"Testable"},{"id":"spn-68644","text":" — acceptance criteria are machine-executable 5. "},{"id":"spn-68645","marks":["bold"],"text":"Composable"},{"id":"spn-68646","text":" — specs reference other specs 6. "},{"id":"spn-68647","marks":["bold"],"text":"Tool-agnostic"},{"id":"spn-68648","text":" — works with any SDD-compatible tool"}]},{"id":"blk-58302","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68649","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-58303","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-68650","text":"Documentation Map"}]},{"id":"blk-58304","kind":"code","language":"text","text":":maxdepth: 1\n:caption: Homepages\n\n[&] Ampersand Box <https://ampersandboxdesign.com>\nGraphonomous <https://graphonomous.com>\nBendScript <https://bendscript.com>\nWebHost.Systems <https://webhost.systems>\nAgentelic <https://agentelic.com>\nAgenTroMatic <https://agentromatic.com>\nDelegatic <https://delegatic.com>\nDeliberatic <https://deliberatic.com>\nFleetPrompt <https://fleetprompt.com>\nGeoFleetic <https://geofleetic.com>\nOpenSentience <https://opensentience.org>\nSpecPrompt <https://specprompt.com>\nTickTickClock <https://ticktickclock.com>"},{"id":"blk-58305","kind":"code","language":"text","text":":maxdepth: 1\n:caption: Root Docs\n\n[&] Protocol Docs <https://docs.ampersandboxdesign.com>\nGraphonomous Docs <https://docs.graphonomous.com>\nBendScript Docs <https://docs.bendscript.com>\nWebHost.Systems Docs <https://docs.webhost.systems>\nAgentelic Docs <https://docs.agentelic.com>\nAgenTroMatic Docs <https://docs.agentromatic.com>\nDelegatic Docs <https://docs.delegatic.com>\nDeliberatic Docs <https://docs.deliberatic.com>\nFleetPrompt Docs <https://docs.fleetprompt.com>\nGeoFleetic Docs <https://docs.geofleetic.com>\nOpenSentience Docs <https://docs.opensentience.org>\nSpecPrompt Docs <https://docs.specprompt.com>\nTickTickClock Docs <https://docs.ticktickclock.com>"},{"id":"blk-58306","kind":"code","language":"text","text":":maxdepth: 2\n:caption: SpecPrompt Docs\n\nspec/README"},{"id":"blk-58307","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68651","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-58308","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-68652","text":"The SPEC.md Format"}]},{"id":"blk-58309","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68653","text":"Every spec follows a structured Markdown format with YAML frontmatter:"}]},{"id":"blk-58310","kind":"code","language":"markdown","text":"---\nname: agent-name\nversion: 1.0.0\nruntime: opensentience | any\nauthor: team-or-person\ncreated: 2026-01-15\nupdated: 2026-02-22\ntags: [category, domain]\ndependencies:\n  - graphonomous\n---\n\n## Purpose\nWhat this agent does and why.\n\n## Capabilities\n- capability:scope (description)\n\n## Constraints\n- Hard and soft behavioral boundaries\n\n## Acceptance Tests\n- Given [precondition] -> [expected behavior]"},{"id":"blk-58311","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68654","marks":["bold"],"text":"Required sections:"},{"id":"spn-68655","text":" Purpose, Capabilities, Constraints, Acceptance Tests."}]},{"id":"blk-58312","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68656","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-58313","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-68657","text":"Toolchain"}]},{"id":"blk-58314","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-68658","text":"CLI"}]},{"id":"blk-58315","kind":"code","language":"bash","text":"specprompt validate SPEC.md      # Validate against format standard\nspecprompt lint SPEC.md          # Check for best practices\nspecprompt test-gen SPEC.md      # Generate test scaffolding\nspecprompt diff SPEC.md@v1 SPEC.md@v2  # Diff two versions\nspecprompt publish SPEC.md       # Publish to FleetPrompt registry"},{"id":"blk-58316","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-68659","text":"MCP Tools"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-58318","spans":[{"id":"spn-68660","text":"Tool"}]},{"id":"blk-58319","spans":[{"id":"spn-68661","text":"Description"}]}],"id":"blk-58317","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-58320","spans":[{"id":"spn-68662","marks":["code"],"text":"spec_validate"}]},{"id":"blk-58321","spans":[{"id":"spn-68663","text":"Validate against format standard"}]}],[{"id":"blk-58322","spans":[{"id":"spn-68664","marks":["code"],"text":"spec_lint"}]},{"id":"blk-58323","spans":[{"id":"spn-68665","text":"Check for best practices"}]}],[{"id":"blk-58324","spans":[{"id":"spn-68666","marks":["code"],"text":"spec_generate"}]},{"id":"blk-58325","spans":[{"id":"spn-68667","text":"Generate from natural language"}]}],[{"id":"blk-58326","spans":[{"id":"spn-68668","marks":["code"],"text":"spec_test_gen"}]},{"id":"blk-58327","spans":[{"id":"spn-68669","text":"Generate test cases from acceptance criteria"}]}],[{"id":"blk-58328","spans":[{"id":"spn-68670","marks":["code"],"text":"spec_diff"}]},{"id":"blk-58329","spans":[{"id":"spn-68671","text":"Compare two spec versions"}]}],[{"id":"blk-58330","spans":[{"id":"spn-68672","marks":["code"],"text":"spec_search"}]},{"id":"blk-58331","spans":[{"id":"spn-68673","text":"Search FleetPrompt registry"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-58332","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-68674","text":"Reference Parsers"}]},{"id":"blk-58333","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68675","text":"Available in "},{"id":"spn-68676","marks":["bold"],"text":"Elixir"},{"id":"spn-68677","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-68678","marks":["bold"],"text":"TypeScript"},{"id":"spn-68679","text":". Formal PEG grammar included in the specification for building conformant parsers."}]},{"id":"blk-58334","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68680","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-58335","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-68681","text":"Ecosystem Integration"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-58337","spans":[{"id":"spn-68682","text":"Product"}]},{"id":"blk-58338","spans":[{"id":"spn-68683","text":"How It Uses SpecPrompt"}]}],"id":"blk-58336","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-58339","spans":[{"id":"spn-68684","marks":["bold"],"text":"Agentelic"}]},{"id":"blk-58340","spans":[{"id":"spn-68685","text":"Specs are the primary input to the build pipeline"}]}],[{"id":"blk-58341","spans":[{"id":"spn-68686","marks":["bold"],"text":"OpenSentience"}]},{"id":"blk-58342","spans":[{"id":"spn-68687","text":"Agent manifests reference SPEC.md for permission derivation"}]}],[{"id":"blk-58343","spans":[{"id":"spn-68688","marks":["bold"],"text":"Graphonomous"}]},{"id":"blk-58344","spans":[{"id":"spn-68689","text":"Learning happens within spec-defined boundaries"}]}],[{"id":"blk-58345","spans":[{"id":"spn-68690","marks":["bold"],"text":"FleetPrompt"}]},{"id":"blk-58346","spans":[{"id":"spn-68691","text":"Specs are published as discoverable templates"}]}],[{"id":"blk-58347","spans":[{"id":"spn-68692","marks":["bold"],"text":"Delegatic"}]},{"id":"blk-58348","spans":[{"id":"spn-68693","text":"Multi-agent orchestration specs define agent roles"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-58349","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68694","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-58350","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-68695","text":"Interoperability"}]},{"id":"blk-58351","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58353","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68696","marks":["bold"],"text":"AGENTS.md"},{"id":"spn-68697","text":" — complementary (codebase conventions vs. agent behavior specs)"}]}],"id":"blk-58352","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58355","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68698","marks":["bold"],"text":"Next Moca ADL"},{"id":"spn-68699","text":" — bidirectional import/export"}]}],"id":"blk-58354","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58357","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68700","marks":["bold"],"text":"ampersand.json"},{"id":"spn-68701","text":" — bidirectional mapping (capabilities, constraints, governance)"}]}],"id":"blk-58356","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-58358","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68702","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-58359","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-68703","text":"Project Links"}]},{"id":"blk-58360","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58362","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68704","marks":["bold"],"text":"Spec:"},{"id":"spn-68705","text":" "},{"id":"spn-68706","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/specprompt.com/docs/spec/README.md"}],"text":"Product Specification"}]}],"id":"blk-58361","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58364","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68707","marks":["bold"],"text":"User stories:"},{"id":"spn-68708","text":" "},{"id":"spn-68709","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/specprompt.com/docs/ux/user-stories.md"}],"text":"SpecPrompt User Stories"}]}],"id":"blk-58363","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58366","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68710","marks":["bold"],"text":"Build prompt:"},{"id":"spn-68711","text":" "},{"id":"spn-68712","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/specprompt.com/prompts/BUILD.md"}],"text":"SpecPrompt Implementation Build Prompt"}]}],"id":"blk-58365","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58368","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68713","marks":["bold"],"text":"[